{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676464-religious-syncretism-between-crone-and-lancea","id":676464,"title":"Religious Syncretism between Crone and Lancea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-24T09:14:30-07:00","id":676464,"title":"Religious Syncretism between Crone and Lancea","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\">Hello! I live in Brazil. Here we have tons of mixtures between christianity, african and native religions, as a result we have different religions. Some of them recognize themselves as christians, some define themselves as part of african and native religions, as well as some versions more pure of these ideas, like catholicism and candombl\u00e9(similar to Santeria). Most of them have some influence from every other religion involved in the mix. They go to the extreme of having rituals from the religion that they affirm not having part. There's prejudice and some cases of violence between them. That being said, how could I reflect such syncretism in my game of Requiem? Should I allow the exchange of some exclusive merits, rituals or even their sorcery? Maybe create some kind of shadow cult between Crone and Lancea. I do like to here some opinions about that.<br /> Some considerations:<br /> I don't like to create new disciplines such as the new sorceries.<br /> I do have access to all nwod books.<br /> My game is built using all splats of nwod, I do maintain some level of separation between all of them using the idea that each one has it's own niche around the human society.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:51:39-07:00","id":676635,"title":"","content":"You probably don't have to go as far as mechanical reflections, like extending access to covenant Merits or sorcery. The Lancea et Sanctum as a religion is already larger than the Lancea as a covenant; it's assumed that most of the vampires who attend the typical Midnight Mass don't have Status in the Lancea, or don't have more than one dot in it if they do. They're Sanctified by faith (although sometimes just paying lip service to it), but they're not part of the Church structure that keeps things running and shares resources actively with one another. You need to be more invested in the Lance than attending Midnight Mass to be taught their sorcery.<br /> <br /> So, aside from giving appropriate syncretic color to the beliefs of various Kindred, I'd just say have a Kindred society whose spiritual community is more fluid and open than the usual. There are practicing Acolytes who attend Midnight Mass. One of the Sanctified priests is invited to the Circle's more important ritual gatherings. Some of the vampires might have a folk mythology that ties the Mother of Monsters directly into the tale of Longinus. The Lance and the Circle aren't at open odds like they might be in some domains, complementing one another more often than they pick fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:30:47-07:00","id":676865,"title":"","content":"If you have access to al the books, I recommend looking up the Livian Heresy (<b>Lancea Sanctum</b>, p. 62), which is a heresy which combines Lancea and Crone beliefs, and possibly has access to both sorceries. It this heresy, or a descendent of it, would be big in your city and actually use both kinds of sorcery, the real Lancea and Crone would probably declare war on it.<br /> <br /> Another option would be Kindred Vodoun as a sorcery (<b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, p. 73) and the few references to a Vodoun covenant in The Haitian Revolution (<b>Ancient Mysteries</b>, p.122).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:01:05-07:00","id":676878,"title":"","content":"If you're using 2E rules, making a Mystery Cult Initiation for the syncretic faction could be a helpful way to give them some teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T07:30:57-07:00","id":677589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676464-religious-syncretism-between-crone-and-lancea?p=676635#post676635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably don't have to go as far as mechanical reflections, like extending access to covenant Merits or sorcery. The Lancea et Sanctum as a religion is already larger than the Lancea as a covenant; it's assumed that most of the vampires who attend the typical Midnight Mass don't have Status in the Lancea, or don't have more than one dot in it if they do. They're Sanctified by faith (although sometimes just paying lip service to it), but they're not part of the Church structure that keeps things running and shares resources actively with one another. You need to be more invested in the Lance than attending Midnight Mass to be taught their sorcery.<br /> <br /> So, aside from giving appropriate syncretic color to the beliefs of various Kindred, I'd just say have a Kindred society whose spiritual community is more fluid and open than the usual. There are practicing Acolytes who attend Midnight Mass. One of the Sanctified priests is invited to the Circle's more important ritual gatherings. Some of the vampires might have a folk mythology that ties the Mother of Monsters directly into the tale of Longinus. The Lance and the Circle aren't at open odds like they might be in some domains, complementing one another more often than they pick fights.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In some cases, this approach would work, such as parades with holy images, and celebrations such as &quot;Festa do Bonfim&quot; and &quot;Lavagem do Bonfim&quot;. Strangely enough, the catholic church is very most cordial is this cases, accepting the other religions presence.<br /> But some Pentecostal Christian denominations aren't so agreeable, they do criticise the Catholics not just by being together to african and native religions, but they condemn the catholics holydays and saints.<br /> They incite violence and prejudice against the non-christian religions.<br /> The crazy thing, is that the pentecostal denominations more vocal against the others religions, are the ones who has rituals of african and native origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T08:25:00-07:00","id":677649,"title":"","content":"The Lancea Sanctum can be made up of different factions that don't work together. The Circle is already made up of disparate cults of different religions. And that's not touching on VII, Brood, or Ordo that can work as religions as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T09:40:35-07:00","id":677681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676464-religious-syncretism-between-crone-and-lancea?p=676865#post676865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have access to al the books, I recommend looking up the Livian Heresy (<b>Lancea Sanctum</b>, p. 62), which is a heresy which combines Lancea and Crone beliefs, and possibly has access to both sorceries. It this heresy, or a descendent of it, would be big in your city and actually use both kinds of sorcery, the real Lancea and Crone would probably declare war on it.<br /> <br /> Another option would be Kindred Vodoun as a sorcery (<b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>, p. 73) and the few references to a Vodoun covenant in The Haitian Revolution (<b>Ancient Mysteries</b>, p.122).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read the Livian Heresy, it would be necessary some customization, in here the african native religions had to integrate some catholic aspects to escape of persecutions, such as saints, but these became part of such religions, so it would be the case of a origin of this livian heresy in here would be the crone circle itself. But that wouldn't cover the case of rituals from african native religions inside the pentecostal religions ceremonies.<br /> <br /> I had already implemented the Loa mechanics from Vodoun to cruac sorcery,but like I already said, I don't like using alternative magic disciplines, except in the case of Gilded Cage and the VII rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T09:48:23-07:00","id":677706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676464-religious-syncretism-between-crone-and-lancea?p=677649#post677649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea Sanctum can be made up of different factions that don't work together. The Circle is already made up of disparate cults of different religions. And that's not touching on VII, Brood, or Ordo that can work as religions as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So this would explain why the pentecostal lancea would give such grief to the catholic lancea, but I still have the question about emulating some candombl\u00e9 (similar to santeria) ritual, cruac rituals, inside a pentecostal lancea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8049-53rv3r1n0","name":"53rv3r1n0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T12:52:14-07:00","id":677862,"title":"","content":"People are hypocrites? Also defectors from convenants will sometimes bring the secrets of that covenant with them. The people who they go to go &quot;Hrrrm...these are nice tricks. We need to hold on to these, but how?&quot; And they come up with some rational to explain why its now okay to have these abilities while its bad for the other guy to have the same stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T00:53:01-07:00","id":678618,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to me because I just finished rebooting my NYC chronicle under a similar premise: that the LeS and CotC would rather the Kindred of New York have some sort of spirituality rather than none. Calling thier alliance the Sabbath.<br /> <br /> And those looking to overthrow thier power being the New Camarilla made up of the purely political Covenants and the agnostic one. The Ordo Dracul being the wild card in this whole situation despite nominally siding with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Even with the Sabbath in power the sanctified and the Acolytes have rules where you do not share the secrets of the Theban Sorcery or the secrets of Cruac with each other.<br /> <br /> It is such a taboo that even the most influential coterie with multiple members of both Covenants don't share their unique powers... It's just something that isn't done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T01:01:20-07:00","id":678622,"title":"","content":"However, having said all that I could see some bleed over in that situation.<br /> <br /> Some Theban Sorcery rituals being adapted to Cruac and vis-versa. That to the outsider the only difference between the Sanctified and the Acolytes is if they use blood for thier magic or a sacrifice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T03:08:54-07:00","id":678692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>53rv3r1n0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/676464-religious-syncretism-between-crone-and-lancea?p=677706#post677706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this would explain why the pentecostal lancea would give such grief to the catholic lancea, but I still have the question about emulating some candombl\u00e9 (similar to santeria) ritual, cruac rituals, inside a pentecostal lancea.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not familiar with the difference between candomble, santeria, and the rest, so I can't help you there. An eays solution is to just make twists to the magics for the factions (in Rome, Veneficia was basically Cruac, but used different dice pool and was more formalized, and had a few unique rituals). Another easy solution is to adapt some of the alternative blood magics in the Ancient Bloodlines book - there's one with poisons, and another to model Voodoo. Maybe adapt Gilded Cage, or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:32:44-07:00","id":679003,"title":"","content":"Cruac is based on movie Dark/Pagan/Blood magick. As such has limitations that I'm not sure the effects back up the fluff.<br /> In another thread I'm arguing Theban in many ways is darker and more monsterous than cruac. So much so I'm thinking of flipping the Humanity rules of both.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut to your point there is a voodoo discipline in one of the bloodline groups. In the New Orleans Book the Baron is developing his own out of Cruac.<br /> If you have access to the Blood Magic supplement(which changes it to a dynamic system), it discusses the motifs and themes of various alternative blood sorceries which were originally done as disciplines. Such as Gilded cage.<br /> <br /> The Blood Sorcery supplement (and 2nd edition picks this up) introduces the concept Theban based sorceries must a mininum Humanity.<br /> All Cruac's cap your Humanity. Now all blood sorcery is corrupted to a point. But is supposed to be darker than the other.<br /> <br /> Decide which of your proposed blood magics fits into which mode Theban or Cruac. Them decide your favored themes and motives and build some rituals.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/105095.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - Onyx Path Publishing | Vampire: The Requiem | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies - God doesn't love me. But He's given me these teeth&nbsp;to spill your blood and these words to speak over your remains.&nbsp;And </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}